**Running everything** (all five files in one directory):

```
python -m unittest tests -v
python cli.py --db db.json receive A 5 --dst L2 --ref r001
python cli.py --db db.json report
```

Notes on the design: `JsonStore` reads/writes exactly the four-key list format so external fixtures work directly; saves are atomic via temp file + `os.replace`. `Inventory` validates everything (qty, ref uniqueness, sku/location existence, stock, capacity) *before* any mutation, so every failing call — including `DuplicateRef` — leaves the store untouched, and every successful call persists exactly one `Movement`. Capacity is enforced against the summed quantity of all skus at a location, with exactly reaching capacity allowed. `ledger` sorts by `ts` with a stable sort, so same-second movements keep arrival order.
